 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
 - CLI parsing accommodates further evaluation subcommands (e.g., `frai eval bias`).
 
+## Threshold Gating
+- `generateReport` accepts optional `thresholds` object (`{ exact_match: 0.9, toxicity: 0.8 }`).
+- Each threshold specifies a metric ID and minimum acceptable score (0–1).
+- Report includes `passed: bool` and `thresholds: [{ metric, min, score, passed }, ...]`.
+- Metrics without a score (e.g., exact_match when references are missing) fail their threshold.
+- CLI `--threshold <metric>=<min>` flag can be used multiple times.
+- Exit codes: 0 = all pass, 1 = threshold failed, 2 = validation error (malformed threshold, unknown metric, or out-of-range value).
+- JSON reports include `passed` and `thresholds` fields; Markdown reports add a "Thresholds" section with PASS/FAIL status for each.
+
 ## Follow-up Tasks
